      "message": "th exit code 0 (output suppressed), confirming the assertions pass.\n\n## What I wrote\n\nExactly one file: `E_unrelated_attempt_1/unrelated_config.py`\n\nContents:\n- `CONFIG_NAME = \"unrelated_config\"` \u2014 module-level constant.\n- `feature_flag()` \u2014 returns `True` unconditionally; deterministic (no environment lookups, clock, or randomness).\n- `flag_state(name=CONFIG_NAME)` \u2014 returns `{\"config\": name, \"enabled\": feature_flag()}` as a deterministic snapshot.\n- A `__main__` guard printing `CONFIG_NAME` and `feature_flag()`.\n\nSemantic assumptions preserved in my own code (no runtime dependency on any contract module):\n- The flag value is a boolean `True`, not a truthy stand-in.\n- Repeated calls are idempotent and side-effect free.\n\nI did not read `semkg_contract`, created no other files, and made no changes outside the attempt directory. Local verification: imported the module and asserted `feature_flag() is True`, `CONFIG_NAME == \"unrelated_config\"`, and the `flag_state()` snapshot \u2014 all passed."
