      "message": "and determinism. The contract's assumptions are restated in code/docstring rather than referenced: report is a pure function of no external runtime state, returns a nonempty string, is byte-identical on every call, and self-identifies.\n- `_section_lines()` \u2014 pads section names to the max name width and formats them as `name : text`, so ordering and spacing are fully determined by the constant data.\n- `report()` \u2014 builds `== report: D_unrelated ==`, a `status: ok` line, the section lines, and a `self_check:` line that evaluates whether the token appears in the joined lines, then returns a trailing-newline-terminated string.\n- `__main__` block \u2014 asserts `str` type, nonemptiness, token presence, and determinism, prints the report plus a `PASS` line. Guarded by `__main__` so importing the module is side-effect free.\n\nNo randomness, clock, environment, or file I/O is consulted, so output is stable across processes. No other files were created; I only ran a read-only import-and-assert check."
